WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.080
AMY GOODMAN: We’re on the road in San Diego,
California.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.410
President Trump is facing yet another major
scandal.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.680
The New York Times is reporting Trump personally
asked FBI Director James Comey to end the

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.770
agency’s investigation into Trump’s former
national security adviser, Michael Flynn.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:25.939
On Tuesday night, Republican Senator John
McCain said the Trump scandals are reaching

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:28.030
"Watergate size and scale."

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.070
SEN. JOHN McCAIN: I think we’ve seen this movie
before.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:36.920
I think it’s reaching the point where it’s
of Watergate size and scale and a couple of

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.239
other scandals that you and I have seen.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:43.489
It’s the centipede that the shoe continues
to drop.

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:51.739
And every couple of days, there’s a new
aspect of this really unhappy situation.

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:56.770
AMY GOODMAN: Speaking from the Senate floor,
New York Democrat, Senate Minority Leader

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:00.039
Chuck Schumer told his colleagues, "History
is watching."

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:06.210
SEN. CHUCK SCHUMER: In a week full of revelation
after revelation, on a day when we thought

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.790
things couldn’t get any worse, they have.

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:16.610
I was shaken by the report in The New York
Times that alleged that the president tried

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:26.070
to shut down an active FBI investigation into
a close political associate.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:32.480
And we are only one day removed from stunning
allegations that the president may have divulged

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:38.229
classified information to a known adversary.

00:01:38.229 --> 00:01:45.890
Concerns about our national security, the
rule of law, the independence of our nation’s

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:51.000
highest law enforcement agencies are mounting.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.220
The country is being tested in unprecedented
ways.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:03.970
I say to all of my colleagues in the Senate:
History is watching.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:10.729
AMY GOODMAN: The New York Times reports President
Trump made the extraordinary request to James

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:17.620
Comey during an Oval Office meeting on February
14th—one day after Trump fired Flynn for

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:23.480
lying publicly and privately about his contacts
with Russian officials.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:28.280
Trump reportedly asked Vice President Mike
Pence and Attorney General Jeff Sessions to

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:38.060
leave the room before asking Comey to drop
the investigation into the—into Mike Flynn.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:42.950
After the meeting, Comey wrote a memo quoting
the president saying, "I hope you can see

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:46.890
your way clear to letting this go, to letting
Flynn go.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:47.890
He is a good guy.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.819
I hope you can let this go."

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:57.050
In addition, President Trump reportedly urged
Comey to consider jailing reporters for publishing

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.379
classified information.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:05.550
Trump fired Comey last week, days after he
requested more resources for the FBI’s probe

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:09.550
into Russian meddling in the 2016 election.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:15.700
On Tuesday night, Republican Congressman Jason
Chaffetz, chair of the House Oversight Committee,

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:21.980
called on the FBI turn over all "memoranda,
notes, summaries, and recordings" of discussions

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.349
between Trump and Comey.

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:29.549
The New York Times report came just a day
after The Washington Post revealed President

00:03:29.549 --> 00:03:35.459
Trump had disclosed highly classified intelligence
to Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov

00:03:35.459 --> 00:03:39.299
and Russian Ambassador Sergey Kislyak at the
White House.

00:03:39.299 --> 00:03:46.569
We’re joined now by John Kiriakou, who spent
14 years at the CIA as an analyst and case

00:03:46.569 --> 00:03:47.569
officer.

00:03:47.569 --> 00:03:53.629
In 2007, he became the first CIA official
to publicly confirm the Bush administration’s

00:03:53.629 --> 00:03:55.239
use of waterboarding.

00:03:55.239 --> 00:04:01.629
In January 2013, Kiriakou was sentenced to
two-and-a-half years in prison after pleading

00:04:01.629 --> 00:04:08.550
guilty to confirming the identity of a covert
officer to a reporter, who actually did not

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:09.830
publish it.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:17.340
Kiriakou’s memoir, which has just been published,
is titled Doing Time Like a Spy: How the CIA

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.090
Taught Me to Survive and Thrive in Prison.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.210
John Kiriakou, welcome to Democracy Now!

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:24.210
JOHN KIRIAKOU: Thank you so much.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.250
AMY GOODMAN: Thanks so much for joining us.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:31.310
Can you respond to this latest scandal at
the White House?

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:38.880
JOHN KIRIAKOU: I’m very, very, even gravely,
concerned about the path that this scandal

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.229
seems to be taking.

00:04:40.229 --> 00:04:44.470
It’s more like an onion than it is one single
scandal.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:50.830
Every time we peel one layer off the onion,
there’s another scandal underneath it.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:54.940
And now we have members of Congress talking
about impeachment.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:05:00.870
I think impeachment, frankly, is something
that is a real possibility, something we ought

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.160
to be discussing.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.160
I think that it’s—it’s pretty clear
that the president has committed obstruction

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.590
of justice.

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.590
And let’s face it.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.600
Director Comey is a player in Washington.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.300
He’s been around the block.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:20.350
Do we really think that he released the most
explosive memo he has, knowing that he wrote

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:23.900
memos every time he spoke with President Trump?

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:28.870
My guess is, there’s a lot more explosive
information out there waiting to be released.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:38.380
AMY GOODMAN: Well, can you talk about exactly
the significance of what Comey’s memo reveals

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:45.110
that Trump asked him to do on February 14th
in a meeting where, according to The New York

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:52.699
Times, he told Jeff Sessions and, I think
it was, the vice president to step out of

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:59.630
the room and then asked Comey to drop the
investigation into his, well, fired national

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.139
security adviser, Mike Flynn?

00:06:01.139 --> 00:06:02.580
He had fired him the day before.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:09.419
JOHN KIRIAKOU: That he asked the vice president
to leave the room, to me, is damning information.

00:06:09.419 --> 00:06:13.919
That tells me that the president knew exactly
what he was doing, that he knew that he was

00:06:13.919 --> 00:06:19.669
going to have to say something that was inappropriate
and perhaps illegal, and he likely wanted

00:06:19.669 --> 00:06:21.930
no other witnesses.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:27.139
That way, whatever Director Comey eventually
came out to say, the president could say he’s

00:06:27.139 --> 00:06:28.139
a liar.

00:06:28.139 --> 00:06:30.270
Well, I think he overplayed his hand.

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:33.460
He intimated last week that there were tapes
of that conversation.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:39.080
I think that the Congress should act immediately
to subpoena those tapes, if they exist.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.630
My guess is they’re going to confirm Director
Comey’s version of that conversation.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:48.680
AMY GOODMAN: And, of course, now Congress
is calling on Comey to testify, which apparently

00:06:48.699 --> 00:06:50.440
he is willing to do.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:56.990
The significance of what this fired FBI director
could say in one of these hearings?

00:06:56.990 --> 00:07:03.830
JOHN KIRIAKOU: Well, it was fascinating to
me, Amy, that Director Comey declined to testify

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:08.570
in a closed session of the Senate Intelligence
Committee but said that he was willing to

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.639
testify in an open session.

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:12.840
That’s potentially explosive.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:19.449
I think what many congressmen and senators
on Capitol Hill expect is that Director Comey

00:07:19.449 --> 00:07:26.060
is going to reveal the possibility that other
crimes were committed, either by the president

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:27.710
or by those around him.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:34.360
AMY GOODMAN: And also, the significance of
the allegation that President Trump revealed

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:40.440
highly classified information to the Russian
officials—the foreign minister, Lavrov,

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.569
and the Russian ambassador, Kislyak?

00:07:42.569 --> 00:07:44.759
I mean, this is not illegal.

00:07:44.759 --> 00:07:45.759
The president—

00:07:45.759 --> 00:07:46.759
JOHN KIRIAKOU: Right.

00:07:46.759 --> 00:07:47.770
AMY GOODMAN: —can do what he wants to in
this regard.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:48.770
Is that right?

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:49.770
JOHN KIRIAKOU: That’s right.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:55.960
The president has final declassification authority
over all information controlled by the federal

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:56.960
government.

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:02.229
So, if he leaks classified information—and
apparently he did—it’s not—it’s technically

00:08:02.229 --> 00:08:03.800
not a crime.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.509
It was certainly inappropriate.

00:08:05.509 --> 00:08:09.930
And if you’re going to leak classified information,
my god, the last country you want to leak

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:11.610
it to is the Russians.

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:13.010
But this goes a little bit deeper.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:20.650
I think this just shows how impetuous this
president is and how he frequently acts from

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:21.650
his gut.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:22.900
He flies off the handle.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.259
He does things without thinking them through.

00:08:25.259 --> 00:08:32.100
And to me, it just sort of makes it difficult
to figure out how he can get through a 4-year

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:35.860
term going down this path.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:40.050
This is—this is one problem, one scandal
after the other, and it’s cumulative.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.909
It takes a toll.

